{%- comment -%}
  Trust cues at the cart, immediately above the checkout button.

  Trust signals work cumulatively along the whole purchase path — landing page,
  product page, and then the cart, which is where the largest single drop-off
  happens. The homepage and product page already carry these cues; the cart was
  the gap.

  COMPLIANCE: operational facts only, matching exactly what the rest of the site
  says. No delivery window (stock is dropshipped) and no returns promise (no
  refund policy is published yet). See COMPLIANCE.md.

  Rendered in both the cart drawer and the cart page, so the message does not
  change depending on which the merchant has enabled.
{%- endcomment -%}

<ul class="sw-cart-trust" role="list">
  <li>
    {%- render 'stridewell-icon', icon: 'lock', class: 'sw-icon--sm' -%}
    <span>Secure, encrypted checkout</span>
  </li>
  <li>
    {%- render 'stridewell-icon', icon: 'map-pin', class: 'sw-icon--sm' -%}
    <span>Tracking emailed on every order</span>
  </li>
</ul>

{%- comment -%}
  Returns fine print — self-enabling, renders nothing until a refund policy is
  published. Material terms belong where the money is committed.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- render 'stridewell-returns-note', context: 'cart' -%}
